From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:53:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: record patches 158 to 165 in the stack manifest

Phase P3 of the IndexedDB redesign: index records written with the
records they index, sequence key paths evaluated into an Array, the
population of an index created on a store with records, the open and
delete requests queued behind a gone global's upgrade let go on, a
request's source as the spec has it, index reads, and cursors over
indexes from their position in the index. All seven edit upstream files
and are tier C; this bookkeeping entry is B, like the earlier ones.

P3.1's fix of two tidy allowances that the P2 review's fold had left
behind is folded into entry 153, whose patch file changes with it; the
patches of the P2 bookkeeping commit were regenerated in the same
rewrite, so that they match its tree.

The P3 review fixes are folded into entries 158, 160 and 163, and the
messages of entries 158 to 164 note them; the patches were regenerated
after that rewrite.

Validation: `uv run docs/ohos-sync/check_stack.py base/2026-11-09` passes.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, with the patches regenerated after folding the tidy fix into entry 153 and the P3 review fixes into entries 158, 160 and 163)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
